**Day 24: PostgreSQL – Users & Basic Admin**  

**Topic:**  
Managing PostgreSQL users, roles, and basic administrative tasks including backups and CLI operations.  

**Learning Objectives:**  

• Understand role creation and permissions in PostgreSQL  
• Perform database backups using `pg_dump`  
• Restore and verify data using PostgreSQL tools  
• Navigate `psql` CLI and basic commands  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  

• Create roles and assign privileges using `CREATE ROLE` and `GRANT`  
• Backup a database using `pg_dump`  
• Restore a backup and verify data integrity  
• Practice `psql` CLI commands  

**Important Concepts:**  

• Role-based access control (RBAC) in PostgreSQL  
• Backup and restore workflows  
• Command-line interaction with PostgreSQL  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  

• `CREATE ROLE <name> WITH <attributes>;`  
• `GRANT <privileges> ON <object> TO <role>;`  
• `pg_dump -U <user> -d <database> -f <backup_file>`  
• `psql -U <user> -d <database> -f <script_file>`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  

• Managing user permissions for database security  
• Creating backups for disaster recovery  
• Automating administrative tasks via CLI  

**Tools / Tech:**  

• PostgreSQL  
• `psql` CLI  
• `pg_dump` / `pg_restore`  
• pgAdmin (optional)  

**Summary:**  
Learned PostgreSQL user management, role creation, and privilege assignment. Practiced database backup/restore using `pg_dump` and CLI operations with `psql`. Essential for secure and efficient database administration.  

